Z||000000||87ECO5||09-05-2001||04:34 PM||||I was able to obtain a couple of old Twinhead laptop computers for a good price (FREE!).  I gave one to my wife (Pentium/100 with 32MB memory).  The other (a 486, don't know speed, with 32MB memory) will be used in my garage for Internet access (to this forum among other places).  The computers came with one 28.8 external modem, one 14.4 PCMCIA internal modem, and Win95 installed on both.  I'd like to purchase an inexpensive CD-ROM drive that can be shared by both machines (not at the same time, of course) but I don't want to invest much.<P>So, can someone suggest a good, inexpensive external CD-ROM drive?  Speed isn't a big necessity.  I've seen a few 4x or 8x drives on eBay but they're either incomplete (missing PCMCIA card/cable and/or power cable, or the price is approaching the status of "those people are crazy to spend that much for that thing!!!!!").<P>TIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||Formula88||09-05-2001||08:49 PM||||Check <A HREF="http://www.pricewatch.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.pricewatch.com</A>  for specials, etc.  In addition to a PCMCIA CDROM, you might consider a Backpack CDROM that connects via your parallel printer port.  That could even be used on a regular desktop PC.  The speed isn't great, but it's probably cheaper than a PCMCIA setup.||||reg||6
